  "body": "Closes #1312\nClaim: mac/mac-mbp\nAuthor model: Sonnet 5.5 (mac/mac-mbp-w1312)\n\n## Problem\nThe profile screen offered a system pull to refresh; legacy's profile has none, only a button (`UserProfileView.swift:544-555` @ `87fe0d1c`; `git grep refreshControl|refreshable` on that file at `87fe0d1c` finds nothing).\n\n## Cause\n`UserProfileView` put `.refreshable { await model.reload() }` on its `List` (gap row #1312).\n\n## Change\nOperator decision 2026-11-28 (#1312): drop it. Only the profile changes; Bookmarks, offline topics and AQ keep their pull (not decided). The ways to reload stay: toolbar « Actualiser » (legacy's button), the `LoadFailureBanner` retry once a profile is shown, and `ScreenStateView`'s retry on a first-load error. Nothing else used the `.refreshable`.\n\n## Tests\n- `UserProfileViewHostedTests/theProfileListHasNoPullToRefresh()` (new): hosts the real `UserProfileView` on a captured profile and expects no `UIRefreshControl` on any scroll view. Red without the change (`lists.allSatisfy { $0.refreshControl == nil }` failed), green with it; run with `UserProfileModelTests` (7 tests, 2 suites, passed) on iPhone Duo iOS 27.2.\n- Hand-checked SwiftLint rules on the touched Swift files: line_length (no line over 140), file_length, type_body_length, trailing_comma, vertical_whitespace, identifier_name. `pre-commit run --all-files` passes.\n\n### Ledger\n```ledger-note\nGAP-LEGACY-VS-SWIFT.md, cross-cutting row « Profile » (line 304, column Pull to refresh): replace « gap → #1312: system `.refreshable` (`UserProfileView.swift:69`) plus « Actualiser » (`:25`); legacy button only (`UserProfileView.swift:544-555`) » with « same: « Actualiser » button only, no pull (operator 2026-11-28, #1312) ». Also in the « Gap issues » line: #1312 now covers Bookmarks, offline topics and AQ only (still needs a decision).\n```\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CEAZJkg4akNJrTQb2i\n",
