   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, mac/mac-mbp-r1445, head 37f99f80)**: REQUEST CHANGES\n\nThe code change is right: one `.refreshable` removed. The profile still reloads through the toolbar « Actualiser » (`UserProfileView.swift:25-27`, which matches legacy `UserProfileView.swift:544-555` @ 87fe0d1c, and legacy has no `refreshable`/`refreshControl` at that commit), through `LoadFailureBanner` (`:44`) and through `ScreenStateView` (`:70`). The only caller is `TopicReaderView.swift:159`. No code depended on the pull. The findings below are about tracking and docs.\n\n1. **Medium**: `Closes #1312` and the ledger-note contradict each other, and the open half of the issue loses its tracker. The issue asks to \"say whether the decision extends\" to Bookmarks, offline topics and AQ, and the operator left that undecided. The note rewrites GAP line 309 as \"#1312 now covers Bookmarks, offline topics and AQ only (still needs a decision)\", yet the PR closes #1312. GAP line 307 (\"Whether they follow #1207's pull is #1312's decision\") is not touched either. Once merged, both lines point at a closed issue for a decision nobody made. Fix: open a follow-up issue (`status: needs-decision`, `origin: parity`) for the three lists, keep `Closes #1312`, and change the ledger-note so lines 307 and 309 name the new issue. Or switch to `Refs #1312` and relabel it `needs-decision`.\n2. **Low**: `docs/lots/LOT-116-user-profile-screen.md:37` still says \"Actualiser\", pull to refresh and \"Réessayer\" reload, so it is now stale (L08/L09). Drop \"pull to refresh\" and cite #1312.\n3. **Low**: `UserProfileViewHostedTests.swift:34-42` takes every `UIScrollView` as \"the list\". If the hierarchy at that moment holds only a scroll view that is not the `List` (loading state, a stale pre-render), `allSatisfy` passes without having checked the list. Require the `List`'s `UICollectionView`, as `ListDensityLayoutTests.swift:56` does, and assert on its `refreshControl`.\n4. **Detail**: the replacement text in the ledger-note drops the cell's file:line citations, while the other \"same\" cells keep theirs. Cite `UserProfileView.swift:25` and legacy `:544-555`. The note could also shift the Loading cell's `:42`, `:70-72` by one line (now `:43`, `:69-71`).\n\n**Verified**: read the diff, #1312 and its decision comment, legacy `UserProfileView.swift` @ 87fe0d1c (`git grep`, no pull), GAP lines 300-309, the `ledger-note` rules (`tooling/docs/README.md:45-74`), every `.refreshable` and `UserProfileView(` caller, and the LOT-116 spec. CI on the head: SwiftLint strict, Pre-commit and Docs consistency pass; the app job is the draft gate. I did not run the hosted test: load average was far above 8, so the simulator gate was not met. The review of the test is static.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
